@startuml kernel-internals
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 40

title What a feature may touch — everything goes through the bus

header
<b>DESIGN TARGET — Phase 2.</b> The bus has send() and take() today; call() is not built. It will **await**,
not block — priority inheritance needs CAP_SYS_NICE, which deployment forbids.
Nothing is wired to the bus yet. See ARCHITECTURE.md 6.1.
endheader

rectangle "**pchat**  «feature»\nholds a PortId and\na &dyn MessageBus —\n**nothing else**" as p #EAF7EA

rectangle "**StateQuery** · **Capabilities**\n«client-side facades»\nassemble envelopes so a feature\nneed not — **not** a way around" as fac #F5E6F5

rectangle "**starling-bus**  «the microkernel»\nports · lanes · **the only path**\ncall() **awaits** · send() pulse\npriority lives in the lanes,\nnot in the OS scheduler" as bus #FFE9D6

rectangle "**state service**  «single writer»\nserialises mutation; owns\n**no domain data of its own**" as core #E6F0FA
rectangle "**ServerState**\nconfig · Connections" as st #E6F0FA

rectangle "dyn **ChannelStore**" as cs #EAF0F7
rectangle "dyn **UserRegistry**" as ur #EAF0F7
rectangle "dyn **Permissions**" as pm #EAF0F7
rectangle "dyn **SecurityPolicy**" as sp #EAF0F7

p --> fac : reads · uses
fac --> bus : call(env) — blocks for a reply
bus --> core : delivered on the caller's lane
core --> bus : reply — Effects travel back
bus --> p : reply

core --> st : holds
st --> cs
st --> ur
st --> pm
st --> sp

note right of bus
  **No component addresses another directly.**
  A feature cannot name the state service, and
  the bus cannot read the payload it carries
  (""Bytes"", opaque). Neither side can bypass
  the other — that is the whole point.
end note

note bottom of st
  **Single writer is not a single owner.** Each box below
  owns its own slice behind a trait; ""ServerState"" cannot
  read a channel tree except by asking ""dyn ChannelStore"".
  What the service guarantees is *ordering* — one mutation
  at a time — not omniscience.
end note

@enduml
